# Code Owners.
#
# Branch protection must have "Require review from Code Owners" enabled for any of this
# to bind, and the team must have at least Write access to this repository. GitHub rejects
# an entry whose team lacks access with "Unknown owner", and until it is fixed the control
# does nothing.
#
# @neotree/core-devs owns every protected path. It has three members, so a pull-request
# author - who never satisfies their own Code Owner review - always leaves two possible
# reviewers. @neotree/maintainers is deliberately NOT listed: it is scoped to the
# org-governance repositories and has no access to the code repositories, so naming it
# here would fail validation.
#
# CODEOWNERS uses LAST-MATCH-WINS: the final matching line decides the owner.

*                           @neotree/core-devs
/security/                  @neotree/core-devs
/.github/workflows/         @neotree/core-devs
/.github/actions/           @neotree/core-devs
/.npmrc                     @neotree/core-devs
/.yarnrc                    @neotree/core-devs
/.yarnrc.yml                @neotree/core-devs
/.pnpmfile.cjs              @neotree/core-devs
/pnpm-workspace.yaml        @neotree/core-devs
# Scanner scope and suppression files: each can silence a scanner for the whole repository.
/.semgrepignore             @neotree/core-devs
/.gitleaksignore            @neotree/core-devs
/.osv-scanner.toml          @neotree/core-devs
/osv-scanner.toml           @neotree/core-devs
/.gitattributes             @neotree/core-devs
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @neotree/core-devs
/.github/dependabot.yml     @neotree/core-devs
